   "reply": "The bug is `xs.sort()`, which sorts the caller's list **in place**, mutating the argument (`median` must not modify `xs`). The function also has two other defects:\n\n- **Mutates its argument**: `xs.sort()` reorders the original list; it should use `sorted(xs)` instead.\n- **Wrong result for even-length lists**: it returns `xs[len(xs)//2]` (the upper middle value) rather than the mean of the two middle values.\n- **Wrong error for empty lists**: on `[]`, `len(xs)//2 == 0` makes `xs[0]` raise `IndexError`, not the required `ValueError`.\n\nAll three are fixed in the current `stats.py`.",
